### Classification toy

Degenerate model: `degenerate : PointedMetricSpace := PointedMetricSpace.unit` (one-point space).

Lemma 1: for any `Y : PointedMetricSpace`, any `A : EpsilonApproximation ε (PointedMetricSpace.unit) Y`, and any `y₁ y₂ : Y`:
`dist y₁ y₂ ≤ 2 * ε`.
Proof: choose x₁ with dist y₁ (approx x₁) ≤ ε and x₂ with dist y₂ (approx x₂) ≤ ε (surjectivity). Since unit is a subsingleton, x₁ = x₂, so approx x₁ = approx x₂ and dist (approx x₁) (approx x₂) = 0. Then `dist y₁ y₂ ≤ dist y₁ (approx x₁) + dist (approx x₁) (approx x₂) + dist (approx x₂) y₂ ≤ ε + 0 + ε = 2ε`.

